<p>Gunmen killed 10 people in an early-morning attack Sunday at a home or ranch in Tehuitzingo, in Mexico’s east-central Puebla state, state authorities said. Puebla’s Public Security Secretariat said the victims included six men, three women and a minor, and that armed individuals shot them. Mexican media reports placed the attack in the Texcalapa community, about 200 kilometers south of Mexico City. The state prosecutor’s office said nine people died at the scene from gunshot wounds and one woman died while being taken to a hospital. Authorities had not publicly identified suspects by Sunday, and federal and state officials were investigating. Puebla prosecutor Idamis Pastor said investigators were examining a possible family motive, while state police, municipal police, the army, the National Guard and prosecutors deployed to the area.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/cRzrJ2F3TAMJfvFQlsV-PmUh99blukAu8dlalLFzXh-FKYNpQB2BauTMpuRDuYp1vVciATVoH5NYts837vJD_JG51utpYT-iSdwG8rUQovJp03B2UrRsiK95W_yZiCfqsdz9zu48LpikPZj7ztqv2C-GDjf4xLaSmQqHhmoWVbM7z6zcIBL5bCtrfPY_MY6NeNnOlzyeGh_Va75KxR0lVfgQHhsfKz3aTiVd31BHpNPY0AkoQdJy_UPYeMUZnolW2Ti7lOAS2FaCtvlYh4509v9QkMiPQqM' alt='The armed attack in Tehuitzingo, Puebla, left 10 people dead.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Victim details: Some Mexican outlets reported that the dead included a baby about one month and 20 days old and two boys aged 11 and 14, while several wire accounts cited the state security agency’s count of one minor.</li><li>Attack account: Mexican media reports said attackers used long guns, entered the property and tied victims’ hands before shooting them, details not included in the initial state security statement.</li><li>Victim identities: El Financiero reported that the victims’ identities had not been made public as of its report.</li></ul><blockquote>Tenemos como linea de investigación que fue un tema familiar - Idamis Pastor</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Puebla state prosecutor Idamis